---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import VideoSlot from '../components/VideoSlot.astro';
import Plans from '../components/Plans.astro';
import { firm, cta, trustPriceNote, legacyPriceNote, priceSummary, pricesEffectiveThrough, addOns } from '../data/site.js';
---
<Base
  title="Plans & Pricing | Tercet Law, Austin Estate Planning"
  description={`Flat-fee estate plans in Austin, Texas: ${priceSummary}. Fees set in writing before work begins.`}
  path="/pricing/"
>
    <section class="pagehero"><img class="bgimg" src="/video/pricing.jpg" width="1280" height="720" style="object-position:50% 50%" alt="A couple side by side, signing their documents together" fetchpriority="high" /><video class="bgimg bgvid" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="auto" poster="/video/pricing.jpg" style="object-position:50% 50%" aria-hidden="true"><source src="/video/pricing.mp4" type="video/mp4" /></video><div class="veil"></div><div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Plans &amp; Pricing</p><h1>Flat fees. <em>Set before we start.</em></h1><p class="lede">Four plans, plus one built to suit. Each a flat fee confirmed in writing before any work begins. You see exactly what you receive, and what it costs.</p><div class="ctarow" style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn btn-line" href={cta.href}>{cta.label}</a><a class="btn btn-acc" href="#plans">Compare plans</a></div>
    </div></section>

    <VideoSlot title="Legacy is more than money" src="/video/russ/legacy.mp4" captions="/video/russ/legacy.vtt" poster="/video/russ/legacy.jpg" eyebrow="In his words" heading="Legacy is more than money." lede="What a plan is really for, and why Russ starts with who you love before any number." />


    <section class="sec" id="plans"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Plans</p><h2>Choose what fits.</h2><p class="lede">The ring on each plan shows which of the eight parts of <a href="/#approach">your whole picture</a> it covers. Below it, exactly what you receive.</p></div>
      <Plans />
      <p class="offers-note">Prices in US dollars, effective through {pricesEffectiveThrough}. {trustPriceNote} {legacyPriceNote} {addOns} Recording fees and other third-party costs are separate and disclosed in advance.</p>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec alt" id="included"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Every plan includes</p><h2>The same care, at every price.</h2></div>
      <div class="includes">
        <div><b>A free Estate Map Session</b><p>Forty-five minutes on Zoom to see your whole estate on one screen before you decide anything.</p></div>
        <div><b>Your attorney, personally</b><p>{firm.attorney} handles your plan himself, from the map to the signing.</p></div>
        <div><b>A fee in writing</b><p>Your flat fee is set in your engagement letter before any work begins.</p></div>
        <div><b>Drafts you can read</b><p>You read every document before you sign it, and every question gets an answer.</p></div>
        <div><b>A guided signing</b><p>A signing meeting with the witnesses and notary your documents need.</p></div>
        <div><b>Clear next steps</b><p>You leave knowing where your documents are and what to do next.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="split rev" id="fit"><div class="split__media" style="background-image:url('/images/pricing-couple-advisor.jpg');background-position:85% 40%" role="img" aria-label="A smiling couple hugging on a sofa as their advisor walks them through a document"></div><div class="split__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Which plan fits?</p><h2>A quick guide.</h2>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li><b>Deed &amp; POA Starter</b> if you need one specific piece in place now, such as a deed or powers of attorney.</li>
        <li><b>Foundations</b> if you want the core documents every adult should have: wills, powers of attorney and health care documents.</li>
        <li><b>Trust Plan</b> if you own a home or other property and want a plan built to keep it out of probate.</li>
        <li><b>Legacy</b> if your estate is larger or more complex, includes a business, or has charitable goals.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="ctarow"><a class="btn btn-acc" href={cta.href}>{cta.label}</a></div>
      <p class="offers-note">Probate, trust administration, elder law, special needs planning, business succession and digital life planning are quoted as a flat fee after your Estate Map Session. <a href="/services">See all services</a>.</p>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec alt" id="faq"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>About the fees.</h2></div>
      <div class="faq"><details><summary>Is the Estate Map Session really free?</summary><p>Yes. It is 45 minutes on Zoom, with no charge and no obligation.</p></details><details><summary>Do you bill by the hour?</summary><p>Not for your plan. Every plan is a flat fee set in writing before we begin. If you ask for something outside your plan, we quote that flat too, before doing it.</p></details><details><summary>When do I pay?</summary><p>Your payment schedule is set out in your engagement letter, in writing, before any work begins.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need a trust, or is a will enough?</summary><p>Sometimes a will-based plan is enough. Your Estate Map Session gives you an honest answer, with no pressure either way. <a href="/faq">Read the Texas FAQ</a>.</p></details><details><summary>What is not included?</summary><p>Court costs, recording fees and other third-party charges are separate and disclosed in advance. Work outside your plan, such as probate of an estate, is quoted separately.</p></details></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec final plain" id="begin"><div class="wrap">
      <h2>Get your number in the session.</h2><p class="lede">Forty-five minutes on Zoom. You leave knowing which plan fits and exactly what it costs.</p>
      <div class="ctarow"><a class="btn btn-line" href={cta.href}>{cta.label}</a><a class="btn btn-acc" href={firm.phoneHref}>{firm.phone}</a></div>
    </div></section>
</Base>
